  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is shown to interact with multiple targets that ultimately lead to the inhibition of 3-dehydroquinate dehydratase. The first pathway links Oblonganoside C to Cytochrome P450 2E1, which is a target of flavopiridol, and flavopiridol is known to inhibit 3-dehydroquinate dehydratase. Similarly, another pathway connects Oblonganoside C to LIM domain kinase 2, which is also a target of flavopiridol, and this kinase is also a known inhibitor of 3-dehydroquinate dehydratase. The third pathway reveals a more complex interaction, where Oblonganoside C targets a tyrosine-protein kinase, which in turn targets a complex that ultimately inhibits 3-dehydroquinate dehydratase. These findings suggest that Oblonganoside C exerts its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition of 3-dehydroquinate dehydratase. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Oblonganoside C and the target enzyme, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
